description:
Design a clock generator that outputs a toggling clock signal (clkout) at a frequency of 80Hz, controlled by the input enable signal (oscena). The circuit uses a counter to count the rising edges of oscena, and when the count reaches the predefined OSC_PERIOD, the output clock signal is inverted, creating a periodic clock pulse while the oscillator is enabled.
module top_module(
    input oscena,
    output reg clkout 
    );

code:
module top_module(
    input oscena,
    output reg clkout 
    );parameter OSC_PERIOD = 12500; // 80Hz

    reg [31:0] counter;

    always @(posedge oscena)
    begin
        if (counter == OSC_PERIOD-1)
        begin
            counter <= 0;
            clkout <= ~clkout;
        end
        else
            counter <= counter + 1;
    end

endmodule

