Design a 3-bit Gray code counter that increments on the rising edge of the clock. Upon receiving a reset signal, it initializes both the binary and Gray code counts to zero. When the counter is active, it generates a binary count and converts it to Gray code using bitwise operations, ensuring that only one bit changes at a time between successive counts, which is essential for minimizing errors in digital communication systems.
