Design a read-only memory (ROM) module that has an 8-bit address input and a 16-bit data output. This ROM is initialized with a fixed pattern of 256 8-bit data words, ranging from 0 to 255. When provided an address, the module outputs the corresponding data word stored at that address. The design serves to store a specific set of values that can be accessed but not modified, making it suitable for applications requiring fixed data retrieval.
module top_module(
  input [n-1:0] addr,
  output [m-1:0] data
);

code:
module top_module(
  input [n-1:0] addr,
  output [m-1:0] data
);parameter n = 8; // number of bits in the address signal
parameter m = 16; // number of bits in the data signal
parameter data_width = 8; // width of the data word
parameter depth = 256; // depth of the ROM

reg [data_width-1:0] rom [0:depth-1]; // define the ROM as an array of data words

initial begin // initialize the ROM with the fixed pattern of data
  rom[0] = 8'h00;
  rom[1] = 8'h01;
  rom[2] = 8'h02;
  // ...
  rom[depth-1] = 8'hFF;
end

assign data = rom[addr]; // retrieve the data word from the ROM using the input address signal

endmodule

